## Greenhouse gas emissions in Mato Grosso by sector (SEEG 13)

The Greenhouse Gas Emissions and Removals Estimation System (SEEG) puts gross emissions for Mato Grosso (MT) in 2024 at **231.2 MtCO2e** (million tonnes of carbon dioxide equivalent). Land-use change and forestry accounted for **54.4%** of this total (125.8 MtCO2e), and agriculture and livestock for **38.4%** (88.9 MtCO2e). The table below gives the sectoral composition for that year, and the chart shows the time series by sector.


